तन्त्रशास्त्रम् {
    # SPRINT 3: Avrtti — Bounded Deterministic Repetition
    #
    # आवृत्तिः (Āvṛtti) — the rule repeats.
    # The count (३ = 3) is encoded directly into the instruction word.
    # This is not a runtime loop with a branch condition.
    # The bound is declared in the rule itself — no branch predictor needed.
    #
    # Proof: Vak write executes exactly 3 times.
    # UART will report each cycle. Final counter must equal 3.
    आवृत्तिः ३ वाचम् लिखति ।

    # Second rule: single Apavada store to Yantra under Ring 0.
    # Proves Avrtti does not corrupt surrounding instruction context.
    अपवादः श्रोत्रात् यन्त्रै स्थापयति ।
}
